 "summary": "The creator advises against arguing in front of an audience that has already chosen a side. He explains that truth cannot convince people who are attached to an ideology or committed to misunderstanding you. Ultimately, one should never seek validation from an audience that is already against them.",
 "key_points": [
  "Do not fight or argue when an audience has already picked a side.",
  "Learn to identify whether a room wants the truth or just wants a winner.",
  "Recognize that some people are committed to misunderstanding you.",
  "Understand that truth cannot defeat someone who is attached to an identity or an ideology.",
  "Avoid performing for an audience that has its back turned against you, and never let them think you care about their validation."
 ],
